    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI'm using tmux to create a tmux session with multiple tmux tabs each loading different nvim sessions.\n\nAll the sessions load, but their buffer sizes (when using split buffers) are distorted, with the exception of the vim session that loads in the tmux tab that is focused on after the tmux session is created.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a session with a split buffer of 2 different files\n2. Save the session `:mksession /tmp/session`\n3. Start tmux with using the following script:\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n\nSESSION_NAME=\"my_tmux_session\"\n\n# Create a new detached session and run nvim directly in window 0\ntmux new-session -d -s \"$SESSION_NAME\" -n \"nvim_buffer_size_distorred\" \\\n  \"nvim --clean -S /tmp/session\"\n\n# Create the second window (empty shell)\ntmux new-window -t \"$SESSION_NAME\" -n \"current_window\"\n\n# Focus the second window\ntmux select-window -t \"$SESSION_NAME:current_window\"\n\n# Attach to the session\ntmux attach-session -t \"$SESSION_NAME\"\n\n```\n\nNavigate to the first tmux tab and you will see that the session loads, but the buffer sizes are distorted\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect the buffer sizes to be the same as when I saved the session\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1095+g53cbf66bd2\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nyes VIM - Vi IMproved 9.2 (2026 Feb 14, compiled Jul 24 2026 20:20:54)\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nOSX 15.5 (24F74)\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty (tmux-256color in tmux)\n\n### Installation\n\nhomebrew",
